# Project: CODENAME

Replace `CODENAME` with this project's codename when generating from the template.

## Stack

- **Platform:** Web (Phase 1 — full AI-assisted workflow)
- **Runtime:** Node.js LTS (pin version in README)
- **Language:** TypeScript (strict)
- **Framework:** [e.g. Next.js, Vite + React — update before first merge]

## Repository layout

```
src/           Application source
docs/          Architecture, setup, handoff (required)
public/        Static assets (keep binaries < 1 MB)
```

## Commands

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| Install | `npm install` |
| Dev server | `npm run dev` |
| Lint | `npm run lint` |
| Test | `npm test` |
| Build | `npm run build` |

Update this table when scripts change.

## Do not edit (agent)

- `node_modules/`, `dist/`, `.next/`, `build/`
- Lockfiles unless resolving a dependency task
- `.env` — secrets live in env vars / 1Password; use `.env.example` for keys

## Workflow

- **Trello** — planning; link card on every dev task
- **GitHub Issues** — authoritative tracker for code work
- **Harvest** — log time daily; note issue `#` in entries
- **PRs** — conventional commits; fill PR template including AI disclosure
- **Pre-PR review** — run `/review-eml` locally; fix Critical/High findings; paste summary into PR

## Documentation

- Architecture: `docs/architecture.md`
- Setup & secrets: `docs/setup.md`
- Semester handoff: `docs/handoff.md`

## Standards

Follow [EML AI Coding Standards](https://github.com/UBC-Emerging-Media-Lab/eml-ai-coding-standards) (adjust org URL if needed).
